      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e87c0a24b04267f0b960603|full_name}: This is more of a request to expose the standardized interpretations of those inputs, as setting up custom actions for every input becomes tedious as well as pointless as soon as people start rebinding their controls.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5fa23c6f47de1a574b67c399",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5b7fb61894211b58b866e8ae",
        "alias": "Binding Condor",
        "aliasID": "65c28068ed6eefce4c52fc90",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/70cde677671ad2efe0439d243d6dec09.png",
        "created": "2018-08-24T07:39:04.453Z",
        "name": "Phasedragon",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5df404cc2072644ac4b5e385",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2020-11-04T05:30:23.970Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 4,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5e8a33402aedbc56a315c9ff",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 16
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Was going to make my own post but found this one - here are my thoughts on how things are right now:\nFor a while we were able to get away with unity's input system - it was messy on Vive/wmr, but it worked for the most part once you had everything mapped out (the spreadsheet posted in another comment). If you used steamvr rebinding to put jump on your A button, it would send a joystick click and everything was fine. This is how things were when this post was first made.\nBut since the update to vrchat that allowed ingame rebinding, you can now rebind the A button to jump without it actually sending the joystick click. Udon has no way of knowing how the player's inputs are set up so it is impossible to accurately get the jump input, among other things.\nAt minimum, we need to be able to poll or receive events from the following inputs after they have gone through vrchat's controller specific interpretation, rebinding, and dead zones:\n-Locomotion (x/y for smooth and a bool for holoport)\n-Turning (single frame pulse of 1 or -1 for snap, or a regular axis for smooth)\n-Jumping\n-Grip buttons\n-Trigger buttons\n-Menu buttons\nIf it's possible it would be great to have the following extra Inputs:\n-Currently active gesture for left/right hands\n-All finger tracking axes\n-Some extra actions that people can put wherever they want using the ingame rebinding",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
